From b10181c4c8b093a9ce11ca2b63597b25bc9e5c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:13:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: Estuary loses #31802, which nothing reads since the
 player information is one panel

#31802 ("RPU metadata", the heading of the Dolby Vision metadata of the frame shown) was read
by DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml ($LOCALIZE[31802]) and by system/hades/DialogHadesPlayerInfo.xml
($ADDON[skin.estuary 31802]). Since the panel of e2a1730 and the pages for other skins of
a8bd9a5, nothing reads it: neither $LOCALIZE[31802] nor $ADDON[skin.estuary 31802] is in the
skin or in system/hades, settings.xml does not name it, the C++ of xbmc/ has no literal of it
(the only Estuary id of that range it asks for by number is 31834), and make-playerinfo.py
takes the ids it writes from the pages it reads. Its entry leaves en_gb, es_es, es_ar and
es_mx, the only languages that have it.

Host tests (outside the tree): po-dups (1212 strings.po, no id twice), idtable (no use of an
id that Kodi shows blank or wrong), validate_skin.py and validate_hades_dialog.py of the
player information, make-playerinfo.py --check (up to date) and measure_all.py (nothing wider
than its label): all pass.
---
